    "q-126764": {
      "dom_id": "question-126764",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Use Euler's method to find an approximation to $y(0.2)$ using two steps of equal size.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $y\\,\\,=\\,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that we are given $y(0)$ and asked to find $y(0.2).$ The distance from $x=0$ to $x=0.2$ is $0.2,$ and since we are asked to use two steps of equal size, our step size must be \n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{0.2-0}{2}=0.1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with Euler's method. We'll start by creating a table that includes the initial condition data $y(0)=0.$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n**Step 1.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the first row) and the values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =2x\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}=2\\cdot 0\\cdot \\sqrt{1-{0}^{2}}=0 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=0\\cdot 0.1=0 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=0+0.1=0.1 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=0+0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $0.1$ | $0$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n**Step 2.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the second row) and new values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =2x\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}=2\\cdot 0.1\\cdot \\sqrt{1-{0}^{2}}=0.2 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=0.2\\cdot 0.1=0.02 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=0.1+0.1=0.2 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=0+0.02=0.02\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $0.1$ | $0$ | $0.2$ | $0.02$ |\n| $0.2$ | $0.02$ | $$ | $$ |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that  $f(0.2)≈0.02.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
