    "q-126766": {
      "dom_id": "question-126766",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given that $|C|\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ use the general solution to the equation to find the function $f(x).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $f(x)\\,\\,=\\,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The general solution is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+C).\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=0$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({0}^{2}+C) \\\\ 0 & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(C) \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of ${y}^{′}=xy$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=0$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+0)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}).\n$$\n\nHence, $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
